    <!--
      The one setting that silently makes the whole product useless: Android
      notifications turned off for Perch. Without a sentence here, the user's
      experience is "my agent was waiting and my phone never told me", and nothing
      anywhere says why (spec FR-015: every state carries a reason and a next step).
    -->
    <string name="failure_bridge_too_old">The Perch on your computer is older than this app.</string>
    <string name="failure_bridge_too_old_fix">Update it there: build or download the current perch-bridge and run install-service again.</string>
    <string name="failure_app_too_old">This app is older than the Perch on your computer.</string>
    <string name="failure_app_too_old_fix">Update Perch on this phone from the same place you installed it.</string>
    <string name="notifications_blocked">Notifications are off for Perch, so a waiting agent cannot reach you.</string>
    <string name="notifications_blocked_fix">Turn them back on</string>
    <!--
      The other silent failure, and the one a Chinese phone hits first: the system
      stops the watch service after a while even though Android permits it. The only
      symptom is that notifications stop arriving some minutes after the screen goes
      off — which reads as "the product stopped working".
    -->
    <string name="battery_restricted">Your phone may stop Perch while it is locked, so a waiting agent might not reach you.</string>
    <string name="battery_restricted_fix">Let it run</string>

